  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 1401.44 Zip line",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 1401.44 “Zip line” means a lifeline suspended between support structures that enables a person attached to a pulley to traverse from one point to another propelled only by the force of gravity.\n\nSource. #12615, eff 8-28-18; renumbered by #13535, INTERIM (formerly Saf-C 1401.331); ss by #14139, eff 11-28-24, EXPIRES: 11-28-34 (formerly Saf-C 1401.40) (see Revision Note #3 at chapter heading for Saf-C 1400)",
